IMPORT prelude

-- Housing Australia Act 2018 (Cth) -- what the Act says to a first home buyer who asks "Can I buy with a 5% deposit under
-- the Home Guarantee Scheme?": who a Housing Australia guarantee can be given to (s 8(1B)); whether the guarantee on my loan
-- is within what the Act allows (ss 10(2)-(5), 12(3)); what the Act itself says about my deposit (nothing: ss 12, 13 leave
-- it to the Investment Mandate); whether I am bound by, or can be sued under, the guarantee agreement (s 10(6), (7));
-- whether Housing Australia's payment under it is backed by the Commonwealth (s 51); whether the Minister can direct a
-- guarantee for my loan in particular (s 14(1)(a)(iia)); and whether I am one of the buyers the Act's object names (s 3).
--
-- SEAT: the first home buyer -- "Can I buy with a 5% deposit under the Home Guarantee Scheme?". Every exported question is
-- phrased as that buyer would ask it. The Act addresses Housing Australia, its Board and the Minister, never the buyer. A
-- Housing Australia guarantee is issued to a constitutional corporation (the lender), not to the buyer (s 8(1B)); so what
-- is encoded is what the Act means for the buyer: whether a guarantee can stand behind their loan, and what it does and
-- does not oblige them to do.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 3 (object: first home buyers, single parents, single guardians, those without an ownership
-- interest in 10 years); s 5 (constitutional corporation, entity); s 8(1)(b), (1B) (the guarantee function); s 10(2)-(7)
-- (applications, consideration under the Investment Mandate, written agreement, compliance, debts); s 12(1), (3) and s 13
-- (b)(iia), (c)(ii) (the Investment Mandate's criteria and limits for guarantees); s 14(1)(a)(iia) (no direction about a
-- particular guarantee); s 48A (appropriation for guarantee liabilities); s 51 (Commonwealth guarantee of Housing
-- Australia's payments, and the s 51(2), (3) cut-off day).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 7 of the Housing Australia Act 2018 (No. 65, 2018), compilation date 11 December 2024
-- (register id C2024C00857), including amendments up to Act No. 136, 2024, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2018A00065.txt. Instruments: the Investment Mandate (s 12) -- the Housing Australia
-- Investment Mandate Direction 2018, which holds the Home Guarantee Scheme's eligibility criteria, price caps, place limits
-- and minimum deposit -- is NOT deposited. Every criterion it sets is an input here, and so is any timeframe it sets. No
-- instrument under s 51(3) is deposited; the determined day, if any, is an input.
--
-- Dates are entered as YYYYMMDD numbers (20 February 2028 is 20280220).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Investment Mandate's own criteria (not deposited; asked as facts); the financing and capacity building
-- functions (s 8(1A), (1C)), which do not reach a home buyer; the Help to Buy functions (s 8(1)(ca)), which belong to the
-- Help to Buy Act 2024; and the machinery: establishment, powers, the Board, the CEO, staff, the Special Account, capital
-- and reserves, dividends, borrowing, tax, delegation, annual reports, reviews (ss 57-57B) and rules (s 58).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the first home buyer, with the design
-- defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public
-- use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Housing Australia Act 2018 -- the first home buyer`

§§ `Who is who`

-- s 5: "constitutional corporation means a corporation to which paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution applies"; "entity
-- includes: (a) a company; and (b) a trust; and (c) a partnership". A bank or other lender that is a trading or financial
-- corporation is a constitutional corporation; whether a given lender is one is a FACT. The buyer is an individual.
DECLARE `Kind of party` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a constitutional corporation`
    `a State or Territory`
    `another entity`

-- s 3(e)-(g): the buyers the Act's object names. "first home buyer", "single parent", "dependants" and "legal guardian"
-- are not defined in the Act; each is asked as a FACT.
DECLARE Buyer HAS
    `am a first home buyer`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `am a single parent with dependants`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `am a single legal guardian of a child`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `have held an ownership interest in real property in Australia in the last 10 years` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The home loan, and the guarantee that would stand behind it. The guarantee is between Housing Australia and the lender.
-- "Investment Mandate" (s 12(1)): the Minister's directions to the Board, by legislative instrument. What it requires of a
-- buyer (deposit, income, price, places) is NOT deposited, so whether the buyer meets it is a FACT.
DECLARE `Home loan` HAS
    `my lender`                                                         IS A `Kind of party`
    `the Investment Mandate provides that Housing Australia must consider such an application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my lender applied to Housing Australia for the guarantee`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the guarantee is for the purpose of improving housing outcomes`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the guarantee assists my lender in its business`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I meet the Investment Mandate's criteria for the guarantee`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the guarantee is within the Investment Mandate's limits`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the terms are set out in a written agreement between Housing Australia and my lender` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `s 8(1B) -- to whom a guarantee can be issued`

-- s 8(1B): "Housing Australia's guarantee function is to issue guarantees to constitutional corporations, where this:
-- (a) is for the purpose of improving housing outcomes; and (b) assists the constitutional corporation in the performance
-- or development of its activities, functions, relationships or business."
GIVEN `the party`   IS A `Kind of party`
      `for housing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `assists it`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is within the guarantee function` IF
        `the party` EQUALS `a constitutional corporation`
    AND `for housing`
    AND `assists it`

@export Can Housing Australia issue a guarantee to this party under its guarantee function (s 8(1B))?
GIVEN `the party`   IS A `Kind of party` @desc Who would receive the guarantee: an individual, a constitutional corporation, a State or Territory, or another entity
      `for housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the guarantee is for the purpose of improving housing outcomes
      `assists it`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the guarantee assists that party in its activities, functions, relationships or business
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can Housing Australia issue a guarantee to this party` IF
    `is within the guarantee function` `the party` `for housing` `assists it`

-- s 10(2): "An entity may apply to Housing Australia for ... (b) the issuing of a guarantee" where the Investment Mandate
-- provides that it must consider such an application; s 10(4): Housing Australia "may only ... issue guarantees to ... an
-- entity in the performance of its functions mentioned in subsection (1) if the entity has applied". READING: whether or
-- not an individual is an "entity" (the definition is inclusive), a guarantee can only be issued in the performance of the
-- s 8(1B) function, so to a constitutional corporation; an individual buyer cannot be issued one.
@export Can I myself apply for and be issued a Housing Australia guarantee (ss 8(1B), 10(2), (4))?
GIVEN `me`                 IS A `Kind of party` @desc What you are: an individual buyer, or a corporation or other entity
      `mandate provides`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Investment Mandate provides that Housing Australia must consider such an application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be issued a guarantee myself` IF
        `mandate provides`
    AND `is within the guarantee function` `me` TRUE TRUE

§§ `ss 10, 12, 13 -- the guarantee behind my loan`

-- s 10(2)-(5) for the lender's guarantee: the Mandate must provide for the application (s 10(2)); the lender must have
-- applied (s 10(4)); Housing Australia considers it "in accordance with the decision-making criteria and limits specified
-- in the Investment Mandate" (s 10(3)(b)) and "must take all reasonable steps to comply with" it (s 12(3)); the Mandate may
-- set "decision-making criteria for ... issuing guarantees" and "limits on ... issuing guarantees" (s 13(b)(iia), (c)(ii));
-- the terms "must be set out in a written agreement between Housing Australia and the entity" (s 10(5)).
GIVEN `the loan` IS A `Home loan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a guarantee the Act allows` IF
        `is within the guarantee function` (`the loan`'s `my lender`)
                                           (`the loan`'s `the guarantee is for the purpose of improving housing outcomes`)
                                           (`the loan`'s `the guarantee assists my lender in its business`)
    AND `the loan`'s `the Investment Mandate provides that Housing Australia must consider such an application`
    AND `the loan`'s `my lender applied to Housing Australia for the guarantee`
    AND `the loan`'s `I meet the Investment Mandate's criteria for the guarantee`
    AND `the loan`'s `the guarantee is within the Investment Mandate's limits`
    AND `the loan`'s `the terms are set out in a written agreement between Housing Australia and my lender`

@export Is a Housing Australia guarantee behind my home loan within what the Act allows (ss 8(1B), 10(2)-(5), 12(3), 13)?
GIVEN `the loan` IS A `Home loan` @desc Your home loan: who the lender is, whether it applied, whether you meet the Investment Mandate's criteria and limits, and whether there is a written agreement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a guarantee on my loan within what the Act allows` IF `is a guarantee the Act allows` `the loan`

-- Even when every condition is met, the Act says Housing Australia "may" issue the guarantee (s 10(4)); the decision is
-- Housing Australia's, and is asked conditionally as a FACT.
@export Is my home loan guaranteed by Housing Australia (s 10)?
GIVEN `the loan`    IS A `Home loan` @desc Your home loan and its guarantee
      `HA decided`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Housing Australia has decided to issue the guarantee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my loan guaranteed by Housing Australia` IF
    `is a guarantee the Act allows` `the loan` AND `HA decided`

-- ss 12, 13: the Act sets no deposit, price, income or place figure. Any minimum deposit is a "decision-making criteria"
-- or "limit" the Investment Mandate may set (s 13(b)(iia), (c)(ii)).
@export What does the Housing Australia Act itself say about the deposit I need?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `What does the Act say about my deposit` IS
    "nothing: the Act sets no deposit; any minimum is a criterion or limit in the Investment Mandate (ss 12, 13(b)(iia), (c)(ii))"

-- The deposit the Mandate requires, worked out from its percentage, which is an INPUT (the Mandate is not deposited).
@export How much deposit do I need, given the Investment Mandate's minimum percentage?
GIVEN `the price`      IS A NUMBER @desc The price of the home, in dollars
      `the percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The minimum deposit, as a percentage of the price, set by the Investment Mandate
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much deposit do I need` IS `the price` TIMES `the percentage` DIVIDED BY 100

@export Does my deposit meet the Investment Mandate's minimum percentage?
GIVEN `the price`      IS A NUMBER @desc The price of the home, in dollars
      `my deposit`     IS A NUMBER @desc Your deposit, in dollars
      `the percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The minimum deposit, as a percentage of the price, set by the Investment Mandate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my deposit meet the minimum` IF
    `my deposit` TIMES 100 AT LEAST `the price` TIMES `the percentage`

§§ `s 10(5)-(7) -- what the guarantee agreement asks of me`

-- s 10(5): the agreement is "between Housing Australia and the entity"; s 10(6): "The entity must comply with the terms
-- and conditions"; s 10(7): an amount payable to Housing Australia under the agreement "is a debt due by the entity to
-- Housing Australia" and "recoverable by action in a court". The entity is the one issued the guarantee: a constitutional
-- corporation. READING: an individual buyer is not a party, so this Act puts no duty on them and makes no debt of theirs.
-- (The loan contract with the lender may; that is not this Act.)
@export Am I a party to the guarantee agreement with Housing Australia (s 10(5))?
GIVEN `me`             IS A `Kind of party` @desc What you are: an individual buyer, or a corporation or other entity
      `I applied`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you yourself applied to Housing Australia for the guarantee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a party to the guarantee agreement` IF
    `me` EQUALS `a constitutional corporation` AND `I applied`

@export Must I comply with the terms of the guarantee under this Act (s 10(6))?
GIVEN `me`             IS A `Kind of party` @desc What you are
      `I applied`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you yourself applied to Housing Australia for the guarantee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I comply with the guarantee terms` IF
    `Am I a party to the guarantee agreement` `me` `I applied`

@export Can Housing Australia sue me for an amount as a debt under the guarantee agreement (s 10(7))?
GIVEN `me`             IS A `Kind of party` @desc What you are
      `I applied`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you yourself applied to Housing Australia for the guarantee
      `amount payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an amount is payable to Housing Australia under the agreement's terms
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can Housing Australia recover a debt from me under the agreement` IF
    `Am I a party to the guarantee agreement` `me` `I applied` AND `amount payable`

§§ `ss 48A, 51 -- is the guarantee backed by the Commonwealth`

-- s 51(1): "the due payment by Housing Australia of any money that becomes payable by Housing Australia to a person other
-- than the Commonwealth is guaranteed by the Commonwealth." (2): not "in relation to a contract entered into on or after
-- the day (not earlier than 1 July 2028) determined under subsection (3)". (3): the Minister may determine the day by
-- legislative instrument, not earlier than 60 days after registration. READING: a determined day earlier than 1 July 2028
-- would be outside s 51(2) and is treated as no determination. A determined day of 0 means none has been made.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the earliest day that can be determined` IS 20280701

GIVEN `the determined day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an effective determination` IF
    `the determined day` AT LEAST `the earliest day that can be determined`

@export Is Housing Australia's payment under the guarantee on my loan backed by the Commonwealth (s 51)?
GIVEN `contract date`      IS A NUMBER @desc The date the guarantee contract was entered into, as YYYYMMDD
      `the determined day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day determined by the Minister under s 51(3), as YYYYMMDD, or 0 if none
      `to the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money is payable to the Commonwealth itself
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the guarantee backed by the Commonwealth` IF
        (NOT `to the Commonwealth`)
    AND (    (NOT (`is an effective determination` `the determined day`))
          OR `contract date` LESS THAN `the determined day`)

-- s 48A(1): money "may be paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund ... for the purposes of payment to Housing Australia
-- to meet its guarantee liabilities"; (2): those are the liabilities under "guarantees Housing Australia has issued in the
-- performance of its guarantee function".
@export Can Commonwealth money be paid to Housing Australia to meet the guarantee on my loan (s 48A)?
GIVEN `the loan`      IS A `Home loan` @desc Your home loan and its guarantee
      `HA decided`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Housing Australia has decided to issue the guarantee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can Commonwealth money meet the guarantee` IF
    `Is my loan guaranteed by Housing Australia` `the loan` `HA decided`

§§ `s 14 -- can the Minister direct a guarantee for me`

-- s 14(1)(a): the Minister must not give a direction that has the purpose or likely effect of requiring the Board "(iia)
-- to issue, or not to issue, a particular guarantee" or "(v) to take, or not to take, particular action relating to a
-- particular guarantee".
@export Can the Minister direct Housing Australia to guarantee my loan in particular (s 14(1)(a)(iia))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Minister direct a guarantee for my loan` IF FALSE

§§ `s 3 -- am I one of the buyers the Act is for`

-- s 3: the object includes "(e) assisting earlier access to the housing market by first home buyers; and (f) ... by:
-- (i) single parents with dependants; and (ii) legal guardians of children where the legal guardian is single; and (g) ...
-- by individuals who have not held an ownership interest in real property in Australia in the last 10 years." The object
-- gives no one a right; it guides the Minister's directions (s 12(2)) and the Act's reading.
@export Am I one of the buyers the Act's object names (s 3(e)-(g))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Buyer @desc You: whether you are a first home buyer, a single parent or single guardian, and whether you have held an ownership interest in Australian real property in the last 10 years
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I one of the buyers the Act is for` IF
        `me`'s `am a first home buyer`
    OR  `me`'s `am a single parent with dependants`
    OR  `me`'s `am a single legal guardian of a child`
    OR  (NOT (`me`'s `have held an ownership interest in real property in Australia in the last 10 years`))

@export Does the Act give me a right to a guarantee?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act give me a right to a guarantee` IF FALSE
